\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(\\sin{x}) = \\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSince integration is the reverse of differentiation, we see that the integral of cosine is sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\sin{x} + C\n$$\n\nWe can discover two other integrals by considering the derivatives of cosine and tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, by considering the derivatives of secant, cosecant, and cotangent, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith these six formulas, we can integrate many different trigonometric functions."] [17592186064392 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0]] "retractions" [[17592186065409 :tutorial/content "We know that the derivative of sine is cosine:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d x}(\\sin{x}) = \\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSince integration is the reverse of differentiation, we see that the integral of cosine is sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\sin{x} + C\n$$\n\nWe can discover two other integrals by considering the derivatives of cosine and tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tan}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, by considering the derivatives of secant, cosecant, and cotangent, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}x+C \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}x+C \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}x\\text{ }\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith these six formulas, we can integrate many different trigonometric functions."]]}]